 ### Dynamic Frequency Masking
-A technique to mask tensor components (density or appearance feature) based on training iteration to enhance high-frequency details in later stages and mitigate overfitting [S13, unofficial]. It calculates mask values using integer and fractional parts for smooth transition during training ($t < T$) and returns ones after training ($t \ge T$) [S13, unofficial]. Introduced in FreeNeRF [4] and used in Few TensoRF [S13, unofficial]. Pitfall: May struggle with intricate details and hidden angles in complex scenes like 'Drums' [S13, unofficial].
+A technique to mask tensor components (density or appearance feature) based on training iteration to enhance high-frequency details in later training stages and mitigate overfitting [S14, unofficial]. It calculates mask values using integer and fractional parts for smooth transition during training ($t < T$) and returns ones after training ($t \ge T$) [S14, unofficial]. Introduced in FreeNeRF and used in Few TensoRF [S14, unofficial]. In the 'Drums' scene, the model may struggle with intricate details and hidden angles, leading to peculiar artifacts [S14, unofficial].
 
